   "textKind": "explain",
   "content": "**Schools without power are concentrated in sub-Saharan Africa:** 12 of the 15 countries where the most primary schools lack electricity are there. Share of primary schools without electricity:\n\n- **Chad:** 97% (2025)\n- **Niger:** 92% (2025)\n- **DR Congo:** 90% (2023)\n- **Madagascar:** 88% (2024)\n- **Mali:** 82% (2023)\n\nInternet is rarer still: in the typical country of the region, 77% of primary schools have none for teaching. The map of sub-Saharan Africa switches between electricity, internet and drinking water. Latest figures from 2020–2026. Source: UIS, November 2026 release; indicators SCHBSP.1.WELEC, SCHBSP.1.WINTERN, SCHBSP.1.WWATA.",
